#!/usr/bin/env -S python3 -I
# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""fake-claude: offline stand-in for the interactive Claude Code TUI.

The test suite points bin/claude-interactive at this file with --claude-bin.
It mimics what the driver relies on, as observed on Claude Code 2.1.314:

  * argv: claude --settings FILE|JSON [--dangerously-skip-permissions |
    --permission-mode M] [--model M] [--disallowedTools LIST] ... [--] [PROMPT]
    Unknown flags are accepted and ignored. --version prints a version line.
  * hooks: every .hooks.<Event>[].hooks[].command in the settings is run with
    `sh -c`, the JSON payload on stdin, and waited for (honoring "timeout").
    Stop payloads carry "background_tasks" and "session_crons".
  * startup: optional dialogs first (no hooks yet), then SessionStart, then the
    PROMPT from argv is submitted as turn 1 (UserPromptSubmit, work, Stop).
  * terminal: raw mode, bracketed paste enabled (ESC[?2004h). A paste
    (ESC[200~ ... ESC[201~) inserts text, CR inside a paste is a newline, a
    plain CR submits, `/exit` + CR fires SessionEnd and exits 0. Every change
    redraws the whole screen (clear + home) so capture-pane shows the state.
  * background tasks: when one ends, Claude Code itself submits a
    <task-notification> prompt (UserPromptSubmit without "source", new
    prompt_id) and runs a turn for it. Typing /exit while a task still runs
    opens the "Background work is running" dialog (numbered options,
    "1. Exit and stop tasks" preselected).
  * transcript: JSONL at transcript_path; on /exit a final "cost-state" line.

Environment (all optional):
  FAKE_CLAUDE_SCENARIO  Comma-separated behaviors, default "ok":
      ok                  no dialogs, each turn replies and fires Stop
      trust               workspace trust dialog ("No, exit" preselected);
                          skipped when $CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR/.claude.json has
                          projects[cwd or an ancestor].hasTrustDialogAccepted
      bypass              Bypass Permissions warning, only when bypass mode is
                          requested; skipped when $CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR/settings.json
                          has skipDangerousModePermissionPrompt
      trust_bypass        trust,bypass
      theme               onboarding "Choose the text style" picker
      api_key             "Detected a custom API key" dialog, cursor on
                          "No (recommended)", "Yes" is the option above it
      unknown_dialog      a blocking dialog no built-in rule knows
                          ("Frobnicator", "No, exit" preselected)
      login               login wizard "Select login method:", waits forever
      login_exit          prints "Not logged in" and exits 1
      stop_failure        turn N fires StopFailure (error $FAKE_CLAUDE_ERROR,
                          default rate_limit) instead of Stop
      permission          turn N fires Notification ($FAKE_CLAUDE_NOTIFY_TYPE,
                          default permission_prompt) and waits forever
      hang                turn N never ends
      crash               turn N exits with $FAKE_CLAUDE_EXIT_STATUS (default 3)
                          after UserPromptSubmit
      ignore_input        from turn N on every keystroke is discarded (N=2)
      ignore_input_turn2  same as ignore_input
      ignore_enter        the first Enter that would submit turn N is
                          swallowed, the next one works (N=2)
      ignore_enter_turn2  same as ignore_enter
      injected_prompt     during turn N, a UserPromptSubmit with source "loop"
                          and its own Stop fire before the real Stop
      rewrite_prompt      the UserPromptSubmit "prompt" of turn N differs from
                          the typed text ("Rewritten: " prefix)
      idle_notify         $FAKE_CLAUDE_IDLE_AFTER s (default 0.3) after each
                          finished turn a Notification idle_prompt fires
      echo_env            default reply reports CLAUDECODE and
                          CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID as the TUI sees them
      bg_running          turn N stops with a running background task; after
                          $FAKE_CLAUDE_BG_AFTER s (default 2) the task ends and
                          the notification turn ends with the final answer
      bg_race             turn N stops with no task running, then after
                          $FAKE_CLAUDE_BG_AFTER s (default 0.5) the
                          notification turn runs as above
      bg_stuck            turn N stops with a background task that never ends
      bg_permission       like bg_running, but the notification turn asks for
                          permission (Notification) and waits forever
      notify_on_paste     after turn N, the next paste first triggers a
                          notification turn ("LATE NOTIFICATION REPLY")
      orphan_child        turn N starts `sh -c 'trap "" HUP TERM; exec sleep
                          300'` in its own session, then hangs
  FAKE_CLAUDE_TURN      Turn N for the turn-level behaviors (default 1, or 2
                        for ignore_input/ignore_enter).
  FAKE_CLAUDE_REPLY     Reply template, default "ECHO: {first_line}".
                        Placeholders: {first_line} {turn} {prompt_chars}
                        {prompt_lines} {prompt_sha256} {env:NAME}.
  FAKE_CLAUDE_DELAY     Seconds of "work" per turn (default 0.2).
  FAKE_CLAUDE_BG_AFTER  Seconds until a background task ends (see bg_*).
  FAKE_CLAUDE_BG_REPLY  Reply of the notification turn (default
                        "BACKGROUND DONE: final answer").
  FAKE_CLAUDE_IGNORE_SIGNALS  1 = ignore SIGHUP/SIGTERM and keep running
                        after the terminal goes away (a slow shutdown).
  FAKE_CLAUDE_STARTUP_DELAY  Seconds before the first screen (default 0).
  FAKE_CLAUDE_NUMBERED  1 renders menu options as "1. label".
  FAKE_CLAUDE_MENU_WRAP 1 makes Down on the last option wrap to the first.
  FAKE_CLAUDE_VERSION   Printed by --version (default "2.1.314 (Claude Code)").
  FAKE_CLAUDE_HOME      Transcripts (projects/<cwd>/<session>.jsonl) and pid
                        files (pids/<pid>, also for spawned children).
                        Default: $CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR, else $TMPDIR/fake-claude-<uid>.
  FAKE_CLAUDE_LOG       JSONL file the mock appends records to, each with a
                        "kind":
      start    pid, argv, cwd, session_id, transcript_path, settings_arg,
               permission_mode, model, initial_prompt, isatty, env (CLAUDE*,
               FAKE_CLAUDE*, ANTHROPIC*, TERM, TMUX, CI; secrets redacted),
               env_names (names of every variable)
      dialog   name, choice (label, or null for Esc)
      prompt   turn, source ("argv" or "input"), prompt_id, text
      injected turn, prompt_id, text (a <task-notification> prompt)
      child    child_pid (orphan_child)
      ignored  what (input the scenario discarded)
      hook     event, command, rc, stdout, stderr, timed_out
      exit     status, reason

Only the standard library is used; Python 3.9+, runs under `python3 -I`.
"""

